concepts.prompt:
Use case: ui-mockup
Asset type: high-fidelity concept screenshot of OpenWhisper desktop settings.
Input images: supplied screenshots are style and product references, not edit targets.
Style: match OpenWhisper's existing dark charcoal canvas, near-black header, midnight navy panels, electric blue selected controls, pale text, muted gray descriptions, subtle slate borders and small blue/purple outline icons. Practical native desktop utility with restrained 10px corner radii, crisp modern sans-serif text and clean alignment. This is a design proposal; example values are illustrative.
Composition: one complete front-facing desktop app window, landscape approximately 1400 by 1000, with a narrow neutral dark margin. Large readable UI type, all content and footer fit. No device, desk, scene, perspective, illustration, gradients or decorative marketing text.
Header uses existing blue microphone app icon, exact brand "OpenWhisper" and secondary "Settings". Native close icon.
Constraints: recognizable OpenWhisper visual identity; credible desktop controls; no invented plan/tier/pricing; no clipped content; no unreadable fine print. Preserve a clear distinction between local speech transcription and cloud text cleanup.
Primary request: simplify the current long Advanced navigation into one unified settings view with just six sidebar destinations and inline expandable sections. No Basic/Advanced mode switch. Show the Dictation page with AI cleanup expanded so the navigation and progressive detail pattern are visible.
Header right compact search field "Search settings" and "Ctrl+K".
Left sidebar exactly six destinations with small outline icons and generous consistent line spacing:
"Dictation" selected blue;
"Meetings";
"Personalize";
"Models";
"Connections";
"App".
Small footer sidebar link "Developer options". No sub-navigation or summary text under sidebar items.
Content heading "Dictation" and subtitle "Record, refine and insert your words."
A single content column with three accordion sections. Use thin dividers and subtle dark group surfaces instead of nested cards.
Section 1 collapsed: chevron right, title "Recording", summary on the right "System default · Ctrl + Alt + R".
Section 2 expanded: chevron down, title "AI cleanup", blue ON switch on the far right. Inside this section:
sentence "Improve punctuation and readability after recording."
row "Cleanup level" with compact segmented choices "Light", "Medium", "High", Medium selected blue;
short description "Also handles self-corrections and spoken lists.";
row "Provider" with selected dropdown "OpenRouter" and small green badge "Connected";
visible amber note "Transcript text is sent to OpenRouter when cleanup is on.";
row "Model" with dropdown "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash";
inside section near bottom a CLOSED smaller disclosure row "Model options" with muted summary "Endpoint, reasoning and custom prompt";
a small text action "Try on sample text" near right bottom of the expanded section.
Section 3 collapsed: chevron right, title "Output", summary on right "Auto-paste on · Live transcript off".
Plenty of whitespace below content. Footer "Changes save automatically" left and "Done" right.
Remove endpoint CRUD buttons, model catalog sorting, total available-model count and refresh from the everyday page; those live within Model options. Do not show their controls in this mockup.
This concept shows that technical details remain reachable in the same page without switching modes. Avoid giant icons and decorative content. All specified labels should be readable and spelled correctly.
